### Try the API from VS Code (REST Client extension). Run the server first.
@base = http://localhost:8000

### Catalog of sources
GET {{base}}/sources

### Create a person
# @name person
POST {{base}}/persons
Content-Type: application/json

{"display_name": "נועה לוי"}

###
@pid = {{person.response.body.id}}

### Phone: start (dev mode returns dev_code)
POST {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/connect/id.phone/start
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "0521234567"}

### Phone: complete (paste dev_code)
POST {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/connect/id.phone/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"code": "000000"}

### Bituach Leumi guided download (parser stub: send extracted fields)
POST {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/connect/work.btl/complete
Content-Type: application/json

{"extracted": {"periods": [{"employer": "אלפא", "months": 30}, {"employer": "בטא", "months": 42}]}}

### Ask a previous landlord to confirm
# @name referee
POST {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/referees
Content-Type: application/json

{"role": "landlord", "name": "דוד כהן", "contact": "0549999999", "city": "חיפה", "gush_helka": "6666-123"}

### Referee opens the link
GET {{base}}{{referee.response.body.link}}

### Referee answers
POST {{base}}{{referee.response.body.link}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paid_on_time": 5, "property_condition": 4, "would_rent_again": true}

### What is stored about me
GET {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/me

### Create a share link for a landlord
# @name share
POST {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/shares
Content-Type: application/json

{"context": "rental", "days": 7}

### What the landlord sees
GET {{base}}{{share.response.body.link}}

### Audit log
GET {{base}}/persons/{{pid}}/audit
